# Files that run on the Linux VM must keep LF endings regardless of the
# committer's core.autocrlf setting. CRLF would break the shell script
# (bad interpreter) and the Caddy/Docker configs.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
.env*       text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What ships to the production box.
#
# NO LONGER LOAD-BEARING (27 July 2026). These rules existed because the deploy
# inlined `git archive HEAD` into the remote script and kept colliding with the
# control plane's payload ceiling — adding the blog tipped it over, and the
# failure mode was a silently refused deploy. That whole mechanism is gone:
# images are built in CI and pulled from ECR, and the only thing still travelling
# inline is four small config files. scripts/deploy-lightsail.sh guards at 90 KB
# against SSM's ~100 KB limit, and the payload is a few KB regardless of how
# large this repo gets.
#
# The rules are kept because they are still correct and still make `git archive`
# smaller for anyone using it. They are no longer the thing standing between you
# and a broken deploy, so a new top-level file does not need to be added here.
#
# `git archive` honours export-ignore, so listing a path here keeps it out of the
# tarball and changes nothing else. The rule is simply: if `docker compose build`
# does not read it, the box does not need it.
#
#   docs/       reference material, read on GitHub
#   .github/    workflows run on the runner, never on the box
#   scripts/    the deploy script runs from CI or the operator's machine
#   *.md        READMEs and plans; nothing at runtime parses markdown
#   geneav.sh / geneav.ps1            local docker-stack helpers
#   geneav.postman_collection.json    published to users, not used by the stack
#   .env.prod.example                 template; the real .env.prod lives on the box
#
# NOTICE is deliberately NOT excluded: it carries the ClamAV/GPL attribution and
# should travel with any deployed copy of the software.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/                           export-ignore
.github/                        export-ignore
scripts/                        export-ignore
*.md                            export-ignore
geneav.sh                       export-ignore
geneav.ps1                      export-ignore
geneav.postman_collection.json  export-ignore
.env.prod.example               export-ignore
.gitattributes                  export-ignore
